+From 706203c18e3ba5e2e0ff2fe5803242bbcf729145 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: lestephen <30328443+lestephen@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 22:06:05 -0700
+Subject: [PATCH 18/18] chore(fork): encode lestephen suffix in manifests, add
+ bump-fork.sh, surface in doctor
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+Until now, all seven manifest version fields carried the bare upstream
+version (9.38.0) while git tags carried the fork suffix
+(v9.38.0-lestephen.N). Installed copies on different machines all
+reported "9.38.0" regardless of patch level, making it impossible to
+tell which fork patches were actually deployed.
+
+This commit:
+
+- Bumps all 7 manifest version fields to 9.38.0-lestephen.10
+  (package.json, .claude-plugin/{plugin,marketplace}.json,
+  .codex-plugin/plugin.json, .cursor-plugin/plugin.json,
+  .factory-plugin/{plugin,marketplace}.json).
+- Strips stale "v9.38.0 - ..." / "v9.38.0 — ..." prefixes from
+  description fields; the version field is the single source of truth.
+- Loosens prepublishOnly regex in package.json to allow SemVer
+  pre-release suffix: ^\d+\.\d+\.\d+(-[a-zA-Z0-9.-]+)?$.
+- Adds scripts/bump-fork.sh with four modes:
+    patch              - increment -lestephen.N to N+1
+    merge-upstream X   - reset to X-lestephen.1 after upstream merge
+    set <version>      - force-set across all manifests (migrations)
+    status             - print current and cross-check manifests agree
+  Does not commit, tag, or push - leaves those for review.
+- Enriches /octo:doctor "Plugin v..." line to split upstream + fork
+  patch level when a fork suffix is detected:
+    Plugin v9.38.0-lestephen.10  (upstream 9.38.0, fork lestephen patch 10)
+- Documents patches 14-18 in FORK_PATCHES.md and adds patches/0014-17
+  mbox files. Patch 18 (this commit) will be added to patches/ on the
+  next fork-docs regeneration pass.
+
